2026-09-14 01:05:26,893:WARNING:superset.initialization:SQLALCHEMY_ENCRYPTED_FIELD_ENGINE is set to the legacy 'aes' engine (AES-CBC, unauthenticated). App-encrypted fields — database passwords, SSH tunnel credentials, OAuth2 tokens, and similar — would benefit from the authenticated 'aes-gcm' engine instead.
Switching engines on a populated database requires re-encrypting existing values first, since the two ciphertext formats are not interchangeable:
  1. Back up the metadata database.
  2. superset re-encrypt-secrets --engine aes-gcm
  3. Set SQLALCHEMY_ENCRYPTED_FIELD_ENGINE = 'aes-gcm' in superset_config.py.
  4. Restart Superset, then re-run the command above once more to sweep up any values written during the cutover.
See UPDATING.md and docs/sip/authenticated-encryption-at-rest.md for the full runbook.
